lar genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 9179, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": 8557, "best_position": 28}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 7609, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 4502, "best_position": 30}, {"artist": "Miguel", "streams": 4196, "best_position": 37}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 4081, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": 3405, "best_position": 56}, {"artist": "PARTYNEXTDOOR", "streams": 3092, "best_position": 71}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 2886, "best_position": 93}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bryson Tiller", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "ae", "country_name": "United Arab Emirates", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 5668, "best_position": 12}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": 3405, "best_position": 56}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": 3179, "best_position": 67}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sade", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "ae", "country_name": "United Arab Emirates", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 7609, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "aespa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "ae", "country_name": "United Arab Emirates", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "The Weeknd", "streams": 17332, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 12938, "best_position": 20}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": 10869, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 9179, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": 8557, "best_position": 28}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": 7695, "best_position": 26}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 7609, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": 7138, "best_position": 45}, {"artist": "Malcolm Todd", "streams": 6809, "best_position": 5}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": 6587, "best_position": 6}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": 5842, "best_position": 9}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 5668, "best_position": 12}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "ae", "country_name": "United Arab Emirates", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": 3074, "best_position": 73}, {"artist": "Eyedress", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "My Chemical Romance", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "ae", "country_name": "United Arab Emirates", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "The Weeknd", "streams": 17332, "be